From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: w478 <w478@local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:52:09 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/lima: start the next task from the IRQ handler

The reference board's Android kernel builds the vendor Utgard r6p0 driver with
MALI_UPPER_HALF_SCHEDULING=1 (its __malidrv_build_info string): the PP and
GP interrupt handlers complete the job and start the next queued one in the
hard IRQ.

  mali_group_upper_half_pp  0xc03926d4
  mali_executor_interrupt_pp 0xc039094c -> mali_executor_complete_group
                            0xc038f998 -> mali_executor_schedule
                            -> mali_group_start_pp_job / _gp_job
  mali_group_complete_pp    0xc03921a4  reads the per-core performance
                                        counters and queues the PP soft reset

In the blob capture, dependent PP jobs follow each other with no measurable
gap: estimated hardware start minus the previous job's finish is p50
-0.05 ms, p90 +0.03 ms over 4274 jobs.

lima with drm_sched at credit_limit 1 needs a worker for that: the hardware
fence callback queues free_job, whose work queues run_job, which does the
cache and MMU maintenance and starts the task. Every job-to-job step pays a
kworker wake-up plus free_job's BO puts - about 4 PP transitions and the
GP->PP hop per Demo frame.

Let drm_sched hand lima the next task while the current one runs
(credit_limit 2). run_job starts it at once if the pipe is idle, else parks
it in pipe->next_task, and lima_sched_pipe_task_done() starts it from the
IRQ handler before signalling the finished task.

What this does differently from the #375 prototype (375-0103), which is
where its remaining sharp edges were:

- The IRQ path only starts a task whose page directory every MMU of the pipe
  already has (lima_sched_vm_is_loaded(), on the per-MMU tracking added
  earlier in this series). So it never changes pipe->current_vm, which
  removes the whole "VM swapped out in IRQ context, put it later" dance
  (375-0103's pipe->put_vm) and with it any chance of lima_vm_put() ->
  lima_vm_release() -> dma_free_wc() being reached from a hard IRQ. All of
  the remaining work there - the conditional L2 invalidate, the TLB zap, the
  soft-reset wait and the register writes - polls with a zero sleep
  interval, so none of it can sleep.
- Anything else is deferred to pipe->start_work on system_highpri_wq, still
  ahead of drm_sched's nice-0 hop.
- The timeout handler drops the parked task properly: cancel_work_sync() for
  start_work, then under hw_lock it takes next_task and clears current_task,
  then drops lima's own reference on the parked task's fence and balances
  the lima_pm_busy() run_job did for it, so drm_sched_resubmit_jobs() gives
  it a clean new attempt. 375-0103 left that fence reference behind.
- run_job drops a stale task->fence before creating a new one, which fixes
  the same leak for the guilty task on any reset (a pre-existing lima bug).
- The GP heap-size fixup moves to the new task_prepare hook, which runs in
  process context from run_job, because lima_vm_get_va() takes a mutex.

lima.irq_start (0644, default Y). N sends every transition through the work
item, i.e. roughly plain drm_sched's behaviour plus a high-priority worker,
for the A/B on one boot.

Risk to pictures: none - no change to what the GPU is told to draw. The risk
here is scheduling correctness, not pixels: a mishandled completion would
show up as a job timeout, not as a wrong frame.

Spike: RK3128 reference #478 (beat-kernel), not for upstream as is.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_drv.c   |   4 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_drv.h   |   1 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_gp.c    |  22 +++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c | 199 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.h |  14 +++
 5 files changed, 212 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_drv.c
index ac8d47d..8148373 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_drv.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ int lima_l2_max_reads = 0x1c;
 bool lima_mmu_zap_tlb = true;
 bool lima_l2_flush_always;
 bool lima_reg_skip_reset = true;
+bool lima_irq_start = true;
 
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(sched_timeout_ms, "task run timeout in ms");
 module_param_named(sched_timeout_ms, lima_sched_timeout_ms, int, 0444);
@@ -44,6 +45,9 @@ module_param_named(l2_max_reads, lima_l2_max_reads, int, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(l2_flush_always, "invalidate the whole L2 before every task (lima's old behaviour) instead of the vendor driver's conditional invalidate (default N)");
 module_param_named(l2_flush_always, lima_l2_flush_always, bool, 0644);
 
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(irq_start, "start the next queued task from the IRQ handler, like the vendor driver's upper-half scheduling; N starts it from a high-priority work item instead (default Y)");
+module_param_named(irq_start, lima_irq_start, bool, 0644);
+
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(reg_skip_reset, "skip PP frame and write-back register writes whose value already equals the hardware reset value, like the vendor driver (default Y)");
 module_param_named(reg_skip_reset, lima_reg_skip_reset, bool, 0644);
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_drv.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_drv.h
index 7be4cd1..f842b04 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_drv.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_drv.h
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@ extern int lima_l2_max_reads;
 extern bool lima_mmu_zap_tlb;
 extern bool lima_l2_flush_always;
 extern bool lima_reg_skip_reset;
+extern bool lima_irq_start;
 extern uint lima_max_error_tasks;
 extern uint lima_job_hang_limit;
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_gp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_gp.c
index feb194d..73551e8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_gp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_gp.c
@@ -126,14 +126,17 @@ static int lima_gp_task_validate(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe,
 	return 0;
 }
 
-static void lima_gp_task_run(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe,
-			     struct lima_sched_task *task)
+/*
+ * Process context only: lima_vm_get_va() takes a mutex, and task_run may run
+ * in the hard IRQ handler of the task before this one.
+ */
+static void lima_gp_task_prepare(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe,
+				 struct lima_sched_task *task)
 {
-	struct lima_ip *ip = pipe->processor[0];
 	struct drm_lima_gp_frame *frame = task->frame;
 	u32 *f = frame->frame;
-	u32 cmd = 0;
 	int i;
+	(void)pipe;
 
 	/* update real heap buffer size for GP */
 	for (i = 0; i < task->num_bos; i++) {
@@ -150,6 +153,16 @@ static void lima_gp_task_run(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe,
 			break;
 		}
 	}
+}
+
+static void lima_gp_task_run(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe,
+			     struct lima_sched_task *task)
+{
+	struct lima_ip *ip = pipe->processor[0];
+	struct drm_lima_gp_frame *frame = task->frame;
+	u32 *f = frame->frame;
+	u32 cmd = 0;
+	int i;
 
 	if (f[LIMA_GP_VSCL_START_ADDR >> 2] !=
 	    f[LIMA_GP_VSCL_END_ADDR >> 2])
@@ -382,6 +395,7 @@ int lima_gp_pipe_init(struct lima_device *dev)
 	pipe->task_slab = lima_gp_task_slab;
 
 	pipe->task_validate = lima_gp_task_validate;
+	pipe->task_prepare = lima_gp_task_prepare;
 	pipe->task_run = lima_gp_task_run;
 	pipe->task_fini = lima_gp_task_fini;
 	pipe->task_error = lima_gp_task_error;
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c
index c5a86e2..6fe4a19 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c
@@ -256,13 +256,14 @@ static void lima_sched_mmu_activate(struct lima_ip *ip, struct lima_vm *vm)
  * poll. That is what the vendor driver does for a job of the session the
  * group already has loaded (mali_group_start_pp_job, 0xc0391fdc).
  */
-static void lima_sched_activate_vm(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe,
-				   struct lima_vm *vm)
+static struct lima_vm *lima_sched_activate_vm(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe,
+					      struct lima_vm *vm)
 {
+	struct lima_vm *old = NULL;
 	int i;
 
 	if (pipe->current_vm != vm) {
-		lima_vm_put(pipe->current_vm);
+		old = pipe->current_vm;
 		pipe->current_vm = lima_vm_get(vm);
 	}
 
@@ -272,6 +273,92 @@ static void lima_sched_activate_vm(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe,
 		for (i = 0; i < pipe->num_mmu; i++)
 			lima_sched_mmu_activate(pipe->mmu[i], vm);
 	}
+
+	return old;
+}
+
+/*
+ * True when starting a task on this VM needs no page-directory change in any
+ * MMU of the pipe, so it is only the (conditional) L2 invalidate, a TLB zap
+ * and the register writes: short, non-sleeping work that the IRQ handler of
+ * the task before it can do itself. It also means lima_sched_activate_vm()
+ * will not swap pipe->current_vm, so nothing has to be dropped afterwards -
+ * lima_vm_put() can sleep in lima_vm_release().
+ */
+static bool lima_sched_vm_is_loaded(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe,
+				    struct lima_vm *vm)
+{
+	int i;
+
+	if (pipe->current_vm != vm)
+		return false;
+
+	if (pipe->bcast_mmu)
+		return lima_mmu_has_vm(pipe->bcast_mmu, vm);
+
+	for (i = 0; i < pipe->num_mmu; i++) {
+		if (!lima_mmu_has_vm(pipe->mmu[i], vm))
+			return false;
+	}
+
+	return true;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Put a task on the hardware. Called with pipe->hw_lock held, either from
+ * run_job in process context or from the IRQ handler of the task before it.
+ * Returns the VM it swapped out, for the caller to drop outside the lock;
+ * that is always NULL when the caller checked lima_sched_vm_is_loaded()
+ * first, which the IRQ path does.
+ */
+static struct lima_vm *lima_sched_hw_start(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe,
+					   struct lima_sched_task *task)
+{
+	struct lima_vm *old;
+	int i;
+
+	pipe->current_task = task;
+
+	/*
+	 * Cache and MMU maintenance before the task runs. The vendor driver
+	 * does the same two steps in mali_group_start_gp_job (0xc0391e7c)
+	 * and mali_group_start_pp_job (0xc0391fdc), both conditional.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < pipe->num_l2_cache; i++) {
+		if (task->flush_l2 || READ_ONCE(lima_l2_flush_always))
+			lima_l2_cache_flush(pipe->l2_cache[i]);
+		else
+			lima_l2_cache_flush_conditional(pipe->l2_cache[i],
+							task->cache_order);
+	}
+
+	old = lima_sched_activate_vm(pipe, task->vm);
+
+	trace_lima_task_run(task);
+
+	pipe->error = false;
+	pipe->task_run(pipe, task);
+
+	return old;
+}
+
+static void lima_sched_start_work(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe =
+		container_of(work, struct lima_sched_pipe, start_work);
+	struct lima_sched_task *task;
+	struct lima_vm *old = NULL;
+	unsigned long flags;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&pipe->hw_lock, flags);
+	task = pipe->next_task;
+	if (task && !pipe->current_task) {
+		pipe->next_task = NULL;
+		old = lima_sched_hw_start(pipe, task);
+	}
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&pipe->hw_lock, flags);
+
+	lima_vm_put(old);
 }
 
 static struct dma_fence *lima_sched_run_job(struct drm_sched_job *job)
@@ -279,13 +366,25 @@ static struct dma_fence *lima_sched_run_job(struct drm_sched_job *job)
 	struct lima_sched_task *task = to_lima_task(job);
 	struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe = to_lima_pipe(job->sched);
 	struct lima_device *ldev = pipe->ldev;
+	struct lima_vm *old = NULL;
 	struct lima_fence *fence;
-	int i, err;
+	unsigned long flags;
+	int err;
 
 	/* after GPU reset */
 	if (job->s_fence->finished.error < 0)
 		return NULL;
 
+	/*
+	 * drm_sched_resubmit_jobs() runs this again for a task that already
+	 * had a fence. lima holds a reference of its own on it, so drop that
+	 * before the pointer is replaced.
+	 */
+	if (task->fence) {
+		dma_fence_put(task->fence);
+		task->fence = NULL;
+	}
+
 	fence = lima_fence_create(pipe);
 	if (!fence)
 		return NULL;
@@ -303,27 +402,20 @@ static struct dma_fence *lima_sched_run_job(struct drm_sched_job *job)
 	 */
 	dma_fence_get(task->fence);
 
-	pipe->current_task = task;
+	if (pipe->task_prepare)
+		pipe->task_prepare(pipe, task);
 
-	/*
-	 * Cache and MMU maintenance before the task runs. The vendor driver
-	 * does the same two steps in mali_group_start_gp_job (0xc0391e7c)
-	 * and mali_group_start_pp_job (0xc0391fdc), both conditional.
-	 */
-	for (i = 0; i < pipe->num_l2_cache; i++) {
-		if (task->flush_l2 || READ_ONCE(lima_l2_flush_always))
-			lima_l2_cache_flush(pipe->l2_cache[i]);
-		else
-			lima_l2_cache_flush_conditional(pipe->l2_cache[i],
-							task->cache_order);
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&pipe->hw_lock, flags);
+	if (!pipe->current_task) {
+		old = lima_sched_hw_start(pipe, task);
+	} else {
+		/* the IRQ handler of the running task will start it */
+		WARN_ON(pipe->next_task);
+		pipe->next_task = task;
 	}
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&pipe->hw_lock, flags);
 
-	lima_sched_activate_vm(pipe, task->vm);
-
-	trace_lima_task_run(task);
-
-	pipe->error = false;
-	pipe->task_run(pipe, task);
+	lima_vm_put(old);
 
 	return task->fence;
 }
@@ -464,6 +556,8 @@ static enum drm_gpu_sched_stat lima_sched_timedout_job(struct drm_sched_job *job
 	struct lima_sched_task *task = to_lima_task(job);
 	struct lima_device *ldev = pipe->ldev;
 	struct lima_ip *ip = pipe->processor[0];
+	struct lima_sched_task *next;
+	unsigned long flags;
 	int i;
 
 	/*
@@ -518,9 +612,29 @@ static enum drm_gpu_sched_stat lima_sched_timedout_job(struct drm_sched_job *job
 			lima_mmu_page_fault_resume(pipe->mmu[i]);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * A task drm_sched handed us while this one was running never reached
+	 * the hardware. drm_sched_stop() has already removed its hardware
+	 * fence callback and dropped the scheduler's reference, so drop
+	 * lima's own and let drm_sched_resubmit_jobs() give it a new fence and
+	 * a new attempt, and balance the lima_pm_busy() run_job did for it.
+	 */
+	cancel_work_sync(&pipe->start_work);
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&pipe->hw_lock, flags);
+	next = pipe->next_task;
+	pipe->next_task = NULL;
+	pipe->current_task = NULL;
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&pipe->hw_lock, flags);
+
+	if (next) {
+		dma_fence_put(next->fence);
+		next->fence = NULL;
+		lima_pm_idle(ldev);
+	}
+
 	lima_vm_put(pipe->current_vm);
 	pipe->current_vm = NULL;
-	pipe->current_task = NULL;
 
 	lima_pm_idle(ldev);
 
@@ -580,7 +694,8 @@ int lima_sched_pipe_init(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe, const char *name)
 	const struct drm_sched_init_args args = {
 		.ops = &lima_sched_ops,
 		.num_rqs = DRM_SCHED_PRIORITY_COUNT,
-		.credit_limit = 1,
+		/* one on the hardware, one waiting for its IRQ */
+		.credit_limit = 2,
 		.hang_limit = lima_job_hang_limit,
 		.timeout = msecs_to_jiffies(timeout),
 		.name = name,
@@ -591,6 +706,8 @@ int lima_sched_pipe_init(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe, const char *name)
 	spin_lock_init(&pipe->fence_lock);
 
 	INIT_WORK(&pipe->recover_work, lima_sched_recover_work);
+	INIT_WORK(&pipe->start_work, lima_sched_start_work);
+	spin_lock_init(&pipe->hw_lock);
 
 	return drm_sched_init(&pipe->base, &args);
 }
@@ -598,6 +715,7 @@ int lima_sched_pipe_init(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe, const char *name)
 void lima_sched_pipe_fini(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe)
 {
 	drm_sched_fini(&pipe->base);
+	cancel_work_sync(&pipe->start_work);
 }
 
 void lima_sched_pipe_task_done(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe)
@@ -611,7 +729,40 @@ void lima_sched_pipe_task_done(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe)
 		else
 			drm_sched_fault(&pipe->base);
 	} else {
+		struct lima_sched_task *next;
+		bool defer = false;
+
 		pipe->task_fini(pipe);
+
+		/*
+		 * Start the queued task before signalling, so the hardware
+		 * never idles between two tasks of the same frame. The
+		 * vendor driver does this in its PP and GP upper halves:
+		 * mali_group_upper_half_pp -> mali_executor_interrupt_pp
+		 * (0xc039094c) -> mali_executor_complete_group (0xc038f998)
+		 * -> mali_executor_schedule -> mali_group_start_pp_job.
+		 *
+		 * Only a task whose page directory every MMU already has is
+		 * started here: that keeps the work non-sleeping and means
+		 * pipe->current_vm does not change, so nothing has to be
+		 * dropped. Anything else goes to the high-priority work item,
+		 * which is still ahead of drm_sched's own hop.
+		 */
+		spin_lock(&pipe->hw_lock);
+		pipe->current_task = NULL;
+		next = pipe->next_task;
+		if (next && READ_ONCE(lima_irq_start) &&
+		    lima_sched_vm_is_loaded(pipe, next->vm)) {
+			pipe->next_task = NULL;
+			lima_sched_hw_start(pipe, next);
+		} else if (next) {
+			defer = true;
+		}
+		spin_unlock(&pipe->hw_lock);
+
+		if (defer)
+			queue_work(system_highpri_wq, &pipe->start_work);
+
 		dma_fence_signal(task->fence);
 
 		lima_pm_idle(ldev);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.h
index 86f456e..6fc40fc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.h
@@ -60,6 +60,18 @@ struct lima_sched_pipe {
 	struct lima_sched_task *current_task;
 	struct lima_vm *current_vm;
 
+	/*
+	 * Upper-half scheduling, the vendor driver's
+	 * MALI_UPPER_HALF_SCHEDULING=1: drm_sched hands lima the next task
+	 * while the current one runs (credit_limit 2) and the IRQ handler of
+	 * the running task starts it, so there is no kworker hop between
+	 * back-to-back tasks. hw_lock guards current_task and next_task and
+	 * is taken from hard IRQ context.
+	 */
+	spinlock_t hw_lock;
+	struct lima_sched_task *next_task;
+	struct work_struct start_work;
+
 	struct lima_ip *mmu[LIMA_SCHED_PIPE_MAX_MMU];
 	int num_mmu;
 
@@ -80,6 +92,8 @@ struct lima_sched_pipe {
 	struct kmem_cache *task_slab;
 
 	int (*task_validate)(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe, struct lima_sched_task *task);
+	/* process context, before task_run, which may run in a hard IRQ */
+	void (*task_prepare)(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe, struct lima_sched_task *task);
 	void (*task_run)(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe, struct lima_sched_task *task);
 	void (*task_fini)(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe);
 	void (*task_error)(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe);
